
  This feature masks the last 4 digits of the invoice_number column in the d_product_revenue_clone table by replacing them with asterisks ('*'), as per data protection requirements. All other columns remain unchanged. Input and output data validation, error handling, and compliance with catalog/table access are also covered.

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" exists
    And the source table contains a column "invoice_number" of STRING data type
    And the source table contains valid invoice numbers of various lengths (minimum 4 digits)
    And the user has necessary write and drop privileges on "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
  
  Scenario: Drop the d_product_revenue_clone table if it exists
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" exists
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should not exist prior to table creation

  Scenario: Create replica table d_product_revenue_clone from d_product_revenue
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" does not exist
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then a new table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should be created with the same schema as "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue"

  Scenario Outline: Mask last 4 digits of invoice_number column with '*'
    Given the invoice_number value in the source table is "<source_invoice_number>"
    When the masking PySpark logic is applied
    Then the value in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone.invoice_number" should be "<masked_invoice_number>"

    Examples:
      | source_invoice_number | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234234534           | 123423****            |
      | 9876                 | ****                  |
      | 56789012             | 5678****              |
      | 399988367           | 39998****             |

  Scenario Outline: Masking with short invoice_number (less than 4 digits triggers error)
    Given the invoice_number value in the source table is "<source_invoice_number>"
    When the masking logic is executed
    Then an error should be raised with message "invoice_number length must be at least 4 digits"

    Examples:
      | source_invoice_number |
      | 123                  |
      | 9                    |
      | 0                    |

  Scenario: Data type validation for invoice_number input
    Given the invoice_number value is non-string or NULL
    When the masking logic is executed
    Then an error should be raised with message "invoice_number must be a non-null STRING value"

  Scenario: No changes to other columns when masking invoice_number
    Given a row in the source table with invoice_number "<source_invoice_number>" and other columns with values "<col_values>"
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then the corresponding row in d_product_revenue_clone must have masked invoice_number "<masked_invoice_number>" and all other columns equal to "<col_values>"

    Examples:
      | source_invoice_number | masked_invoice_number | col_values                                |
      | 1234234534           | 123423****            | {"product_id": 9231, "amount": 99.00}     |
      | 9876                 | ****                  | {"product_id": 8782, "amount": 115.7}     |

  Scenario: Access restriction error on Unity Catalog
    Given the user lacks DROP or CREATE privileges on "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    When the PySpark logic is executed
    Then an error message is returned "Permission denied for DROP or CREATE on table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"

  Scenario Outline: Validate masked values do not contain digits in last 4 characters
    Given the invoice_number in d_product_revenue_clone is "<masked_invoice_number>"
    When examining the last 4 characters of the field
    Then all characters in the last 4 positions must be "*"

    Examples:
      | masked_invoice_number |
      | 123423****           |
      | ****                 |
      | 5678****             |
      | 39998****            |